3. Platform Categories

For purposes of this License, eligible competitive ranks are divided into the following platform categories:

(a) PC; and

(b) Console (Cross-Platform Enabled).

A competitive rank may only be compared against a rank belonging to the same platform category.

PC ranks may only be compared against PC ranks.

Eligible console ranks may only be compared against eligible console ranks.

PC ranks and console ranks are never directly comparable for purposes of this License.

4. Console Platform Category

All supported console platforms shall be treated as a single combined platform category, provided that the relevant competitive rank was earned while cross-platform functionality applicable to competitive matchmaking was enabled.

This combined Console (Cross-Platform Enabled) category includes, where supported by Overwatch, ranks earned on PlayStation, Xbox, Nintendo hardware, or any successor console platform.

A person using one eligible console platform may compare their rank against the copyright holder's eligible console rank even if the two ranks were earned on different console hardware.

For example, an eligible rank earned on PlayStation may be compared against an eligible rank earned on Xbox.

The specific console manufacturer or hardware family does not affect the comparison once the rank qualifies for the Console (Cross-Platform Enabled) category.

5. Ineligible Console Ranks

A competitive rank earned on a console while cross-platform functionality applicable to competitive matchmaking was disabled is ineligible for all purposes under this License.

An ineligible console rank:

(a) shall not be used to establish a Higher Competitive Rank;

(b) shall not be used as the copyright holder's reference rank;

(c) shall not be compared against a PC rank;

(d) shall not be compared against an eligible console rank; and

(e) shall be treated as though no qualifying rank were available for that competitive category.

A player may not establish permission to modify the Software by using a competitive rank obtained from a console matchmaking environment isolated by disabling cross-platform functionality.

If available evidence does not reasonably establish whether a console rank was earned with the required cross-platform functionality enabled, the person relying upon that rank bears the burden of showing that the rank is eligible under this Section.

6. Open Queue

An Open Queue competitive rank may only be compared with another Open Queue competitive rank.

The person's Open Queue rank shall be compared against the copyright holder's Open Queue rank within the same platform category.

Accordingly:

(a) a PC Open Queue rank may only be compared against a PC Open Queue rank; and

(b) an eligible Console (Cross-Platform Enabled) Open Queue rank may only be compared against another eligible Console (Cross-Platform Enabled) Open Queue rank.

A person qualifies under Open Queue only if that person's Open Queue rank is strictly higher than the copyright holder's applicable Open Queue rank.

An Open Queue rank may not be compared against any Role Queue rank.

7. Role Queue

For Role Queue, the specific roles played by the two players do not need to match.

For each player, determine that player's highest eligible Role Queue rank among all ranked roles available to that player, including Tank, Damage, and Support.

The person's highest Role Queue rank shall then be compared against the copyright holder's highest Role Queue rank within the same platform category.

For example, if:

- the copyright holder's highest eligible Role Queue rank is Master on Support; and
- another person's highest eligible Role Queue rank is Grandmaster on Tank,

the other person has the higher Role Queue rank, regardless of the fact that the two highest ranks were earned on different roles.

A player's lower-ranked roles are irrelevant once that player's highest eligible Role Queue rank has been established.

A person qualifies under Role Queue only if that person's highest applicable Role Queue rank is strictly higher than the copyright holder's highest applicable Role Queue rank.

A Role Queue rank may not be compared against an Open Queue rank.

For console players, only eligible Console (Cross-Platform Enabled) Role Queue ranks may be considered.

8. Independent Qualification Through Either Queue

A person is considered to have a Higher Competitive Rank if the person qualifies under either:

(a) Open Queue under Section 6; or

(b) Role Queue under Section 7.

It is not necessary to have a higher rank in both queue types.

9. Strictly Higher Rank

A rank is "higher" only if it is strictly higher under the competitive ranking system used by Overwatch at the relevant time.

An equal rank does not qualify.

Where ranks consist of both a tier and a division, both shall be considered according to the ordering used by Overwatch.

Where the game uses divisions numbered from 5 through 1 within a tier, Division 1 shall be considered higher than Division 2, Division 2 higher than Division 3, and so forth.

Grandmaster, Champion, Top 500, and any successor or replacement ranking designation shall be interpreted according to the ordinary competitive ordering used by Overwatch at the relevant time.

10. General Season Rule

